<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vienna Awards</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1938–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> Awards were two arbitrations by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> that returned territory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-vienna-award">First Vienna Award</a> of 2 November 1938 gave Hungary southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Carpathian Ruthenia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, and the Second Vienna Award of 30 August 1940 gave it northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. Both were annulled by the peace treaties of 1947.</p></div>
